From 672970bcf4ba920c70dfe013423b2c14a6b5af09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:24:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Shorten the descriptions of the scanner information
 and OpenScanner

Keep to what an application needs to know, and leave the reasons to the
proposal. The scanner id was said to be stable across sessions, which it
is not.
---
 data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml | 36 +++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
index 95cb3e5..90544b3 100644
--- a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
+++ b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
@@ -112,9 +112,8 @@
         @scanners: Array of scanner id and information vardict
 
         Lists the scanners this application has been granted access to and
-        that are currently available. The scanner id is opaque and stable
-        across sessions for the same physical scanner where the backend
-        allows it. Applications must not construct ids.
+        that are currently available. The scanner id is opaque: do not construct
+        ids, or keep them for the next run.
 
         A physical scanner is listed once, however many drivers find it, as
         a network scanner is by both an eSCL and a vendor driver. The portal
@@ -136,9 +135,8 @@
 
         * ``backend`` (``s``)
 
-          The SANE backend that drives the scanner, such as ``plustek8200i``.
-          Applications match device quirks on it: the scanner id is opaque and
-          cannot be used for that.
+          The SANE backend that drives the scanner, such as
+          ``plustek8200i``, for matching device quirks.
 
         * ``kind`` (``s``)
 
@@ -152,21 +150,15 @@
 
         * ``capabilities`` (``as``)
 
-          Same vocabulary as ``required_capabilities`` in SelectScanners().
-          The portal sets them, not the driver: it knows which scanners are
-          for film, by USB id or by product line, and assumes that a scanner
-          it does not know to be for film only is for documents, so it has
-          ``flatbed`` unless its driver says it is a sheet feeder. They are
-          reliable enough to filter on; GetOptions() is still authoritative
-          for what an opened scanner can do.
+          What the scanner can do, with the values of
+          ``required_capabilities`` in SelectScanners(). The portal sets
+          them. GetOptions() is authoritative for an opened scanner.
 
         * ``buttons`` (``as``)
 
-          The buttons of the scanner that the portal can report, with
-          ButtonEvent, by the names the portal gives them: ``scan``,
-          ``copy``, ``email``, ``pdf``, ``file`` or ``extra``. Empty when
-          the scanner has none, or its driver is not one the portal knows
-          the buttons of.
+          The buttons the portal can report with ButtonEvent: any of
+          ``scan``, ``copy``, ``email``, ``pdf``, ``file`` and ``extra``.
+          Empty if there are none.
 
         * ``available`` (``b``)
 
@@ -195,11 +187,9 @@
           token is already taken.
 
         Opens a granted scanner and takes the host's exclusive lock on it.
-        Opening can take a long time: seconds for a scanner on USB (lamp
-        warm-up, calibration), and on a network scanner through ``airscan``
-        more than D-Bus's default call timeout of 25 seconds. The call is
-        therefore a request: it returns at once, and the outcome comes as a
-        Response. The call itself fails with
+        Opening can take longer than D-Bus's call timeout, so this is a
+        request: it returns at once, and the outcome comes as a Response. The
+        call itself fails with
         ``org.freedesktop.portal.Error.NotAllowed`` if the id was not
         granted. Close the request to give up; no Response follows.
 
